      m_Calls: []
  m_text: <b>The Thar Desert</b>, also known as the Great Indian Desert, lies to
    the west of the Aravalli Hills. It is a sandy plain with widespread sand dunes
    (barchans) shaped by strong desert winds. The region receives less than 150 mm
    rainfall annually, has an arid climate, and sparse thorny vegetation. The soil
    is sandy, saline, and poor in fertility, yet supports hardy crops like millets
    and camel grazing in some oases.
